James Nojek modified the integrated method on 2026-11-14. The changes use
our own grouped OOF YOLO11s proposals, individually supplied MAGFiLO mask
views, the accepted TorchVision V1 two-channel initialization, exact native
mask assembly and a frozen reproducible inference pipeline. The integrated
detector and refiner software is under AGPL-3.0 (LICENSE-AGPL-3.0).
The independent compact U-Net source remains under MIT (LICENSE).
Training and inference corresponding source ships in this repository.

The fitted refiner had no third-party solar weights or predictions. Its
ResNet18 donor was TorchVision ResNet18_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1, file
resnet18-f37072fd.pth (46,830,571 bytes; SHA-256
f37072fd47e89c5e827621c5baffa7500819f7896bbacec160b1a16c560e07ec).
Training discards its classifier, adapts the first convolution to two
channels and fine-tunes the fitted encoder and decoder on supplied solar
training inputs. The original donor is excluded. Inference constructs
SMP 0.5.0 with encoder_weights=None and loads the fitted state offline.

TorchVision software is BSD-3-Clause and SMP software is MIT. Their
source licenses do not establish the terms of the pretrained tensors.
The fitted state's provenance includes the initializer and applicable
donor or data terms remain applicable.
